# Gate 0 Flash fixtures

`shared-object-avm1.swf` and `RuffleTest.sol` are copied from the Ruffle v0.4.1
test suite:

- Source: <https://github.com/ruffle-rs/ruffle/tree/v0.4.1/tests/tests/swfs/avm1/shared_object>
- Upstream SWF name: `test.swf`
- SWF SHA-256: `1a215bd4d1f1b6833267216650d8b1db94b42b9f72fb6489e18a65c229411b7c`
- SOL SHA-256: `f680967f67a440d153d63cfd00c89ece1c0770d79531d51003afa3131758b978`
- License: Apache-2.0 or MIT, matching the upstream Ruffle repository

The AVM1 fixture writes a `RuffleTest` SharedObject on its first run and reads it
on its second run. This makes the fixture deterministic evidence for the macOS
WKWebView/Ruffle persistence bridge.

